WEBVTT


00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.212
Here you go, sir.


00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:28.220
Thank you,
pretty lady.


00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.856
You got what I need?


00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.900
Yeah,
but we have a problem.


00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.867
NELSON: Talk to me.
I think he knows.


00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.096
Why?


00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.162
I'm being followed
by one of his people.


00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.003
Stay where you're at.
I'm coming to you.


00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:52.044
I'm by my yacht. It's at
pier three. Please hurry.


00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:15.125
FBl! Drop your weapon!


00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.801
Help!


00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.977
THUG: Get in.
Get in now!


00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.037
MILES: No!


00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.481
THUG: Come on,
let's go!


00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.295
MILES: Help! Help!


00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.371
No. Don't shoot.


00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.957
See if they can intercept
it before it gets out to sea.


00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:21.967
Four men on board,
one of them has been shot.


00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:24.702
Correct.


00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.366
Ah, Rebecca, the witness on
the L train, what was his name?


00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.766
Kryling, with a K,


00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:34.705
Robert L. He has a wife,
two kids, lives in Brooklyn.


00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:39.411
Looks like they're
gonna nail him.


00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.007
I hope so.


00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.674
Investment and risk
goes hand in hand.


00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.183
This is a politically
motivated


00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:47.116
prosecution
that will fail.


00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.847
There is no evidence
that I


00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:52.084
or my company have
committed any wrongdoing.


00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.955
A billion dollars
in pension funds


00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:56.655
just vanishes and you
didn't do anything wrong?


00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.754
You lying sack of crap.


00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.293
Oh, by the way,
Hank's looking for you.


00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:04.336
He's usually on his third cup of
coffee before he can handle me.


00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:06.167
I think it's something to
do with the Sakwin story.


00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:07.433
Sounded urgent.


00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:10.442
Well, he can't fire me. I know
where all the bodies are buried.


00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.172
Yeah, 'cause you're the
one who put them there.


00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:15.009
They are considering pressing charges.


00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.605
This is
preposterous!


00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:18.082
This is a felony.


00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.812
No, what Sakwin
did is a felony.


00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.547
Their CEO is going
to jail for 10 years


00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:23.179
because we did
your job for you.


00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:24.723
Well, unlike you,
Mrs. Scott,


00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:27.589
the district attorney's
office is constrained by laws.


00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.424
Hacking into other people's
computer files is a felony.


00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:33.727
They were environmental
polluters on a massive scale!


00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:34.892
Hell, that doesn't
give you the right


00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.958
to access
personal information.


00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.799
Can you prove it was her?


00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:42.334
We traced it to
her desk, her computer.


00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.467
Plenty of people have
access to her computer.


00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:45.670
Could've been anybody.


00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:47.269
I only access
public files.


00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:49.372
If someone else was
using my computer, then...


00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.110
Look, this is just
a warning, okay?


00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:53.948
This happens again,
I will make it my life's work


00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.578
to shut this place down.


00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:57.150
Duly noted.


00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.815
It won't happen again.


00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.458
Why am I wasting my time?


00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:03.084
Huh?


00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:06.290
Go to hell,
both of you!


00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.598
Sorry.


00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:15.932
You're fired.
I quit!


00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:17.839
Get back to work.
Yes, sir.


00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.172
This ever happens again...


00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:20.712
It won't.


00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:56.105
Oscar.


00:06:57.316 --> 00:07:00.149
Oh, good boy,
good boy!


00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.119
Yeah.


00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:04.445
All right.


00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:12.826
Who is it?


00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:14.025
NELSON: FBl.


00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.158
What?


00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:19.000
My name is Agent John Nelson,
International Operations.


00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:20.966
I have ID.


00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.239
Look, if you have any more questions


00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:29.304
about Sakwin Oil,
you can call my boss.


00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:31.782
This is not about
Sakwin Oil, Mrs. Scott.


00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:34.115
It's important
that I speak to you.


00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:40.250
May I come in?


00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:44.661
I was gonna make some
tea. Would you like some?


00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.197
No, thank you.


00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:48.622
I read your stuff.


00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:51.428
You like it?


00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:53.233
You could've been a cop.


00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:56.300
I'll take that
as a compliment.


00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:58.574
So what do you
want with me?


00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:01.243
Is this your husband?


00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.347
Yes.


00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:08.251
I'm sorry to inform you
that your husband is dead.


00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:11.921
I'm aware of that.


00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:13.583
He died two years ago.


00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:15.820
He didn't die
two years ago.


00:08:15.895 --> 00:08:17.658
He was killed
three nights ago.


00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.698
That's ridiculous.
Your husband,


00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:22.427
formerly known as
Miles Scott,


00:08:22.502 --> 00:08:24.834
currently using the
alias Dennis Archer,


00:08:24.904 --> 00:08:26.303
was murdered
three nights ago.


00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:28.363
Is the FBl always
this incompetent?


00:08:28.441 --> 00:08:31.308
My husband died in an auto
accident two years ago.


00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:33.208
I know this because
I was at his funeral.


00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:35.247
Was it a closed casket?
Yes.


00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:37.214
He was burned badly.


00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:40.218
Has he tried to contact
you in the last two years?


00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:41.514
You're not listening.


00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:44.681
My husband died
two years ago.


00:08:46.058 --> 00:08:48.788
These photos were taken
in the last three months.


00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.764
How do you explain that?


00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:57.131
I... I don't know.


00:08:57.203 --> 00:08:59.398
We also have a match
on his fingerprints.


00:08:59.472 --> 00:09:00.700
I'm sorry, Mrs. Scott.


00:09:00.773 --> 00:09:03.207
I wouldn't be here if I
wasn't absolutely certain.


00:09:09.982 --> 00:09:11.472
My God.


00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.533
I realize this
is distressing,


00:09:30.603 --> 00:09:33.094
but I have to ask
you some questions.


00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:36.505
When was the last
time you saw your...


00:09:36.576 --> 00:09:38.407
How did Miles die?


00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:41.112
He was shot.


00:09:46.953 --> 00:09:48.477
Where did this happen?


00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:49.816
Australia.


00:09:49.889 --> 00:09:51.516
Australia?


00:09:52.191 --> 00:09:55.058
Sanctuary Cove,
east coast.


00:09:55.294 --> 00:09:58.058
It's a resort town
kinda like the Hamptons.


00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:00.530
And you're absolutely
certain it was him?


00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.261
I saw it happen.


00:10:02.335 --> 00:10:03.393
You were there?


00:10:04.003 --> 00:10:07.336
We were about to put
him in witness protection


00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:09.202
until somebody
got to him first.


00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:11.072
Witness protection, why?


00:10:11.143 --> 00:10:14.306
He was involved in some pretty
serious financial crimes.


00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.779
I can't tell you
any more than that.


00:10:15.848 --> 00:10:17.543
Miles was a tax accountant.


00:10:17.617 --> 00:10:20.450
His clients were hardly
what you'd call wealthy.


00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:21.918
Well, he was about to
give us all the evidence


00:10:21.988 --> 00:10:23.683
we need in exchange
for immunity.


00:10:24.724 --> 00:10:26.214
Evidence for what?


00:10:28.961 --> 00:10:31.020
No, there must be
some mistake.


00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:33.498
Can you think of any reason
why your husband


00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:35.500
would wanna fake
his own death?


00:10:35.568 --> 00:10:37.866
Was he in some
kind of trouble?


00:10:37.937 --> 00:10:41.498
No, Miles
was doing well.


00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:44.901
His clients trusted him,
everyone loved him.


00:10:46.912 --> 00:10:48.743
Mrs. Scott,
if there is anything


00:10:48.814 --> 00:10:50.145
you're not telling me...


00:10:50.216 --> 00:10:51.706
What?


00:10:52.618 --> 00:10:54.279
Why would I lie?


00:10:56.856 --> 00:11:00.155
You don't think I had anything
to do with this, do you?


00:11:00.226 --> 00:11:01.215
Did you?


00:11:01.293 --> 00:11:02.988
Of course not!


00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:06.624
I'm just required to
ask these questions.


00:11:12.738 --> 00:11:13.898
I need you to leave.


00:11:15.441 --> 00:11:17.306
I need some time
to process this.


00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:19.007
Of course.


00:11:20.179 --> 00:11:22.773
I'm leaving for
Australia tonight,


00:11:22.848 --> 00:11:25.612
so another agent will take your
statement in a couple of days.


00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:27.653
If you can think of
anything that might help,


00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.210
please don't
hesitate to call.


00:11:29.288 --> 00:11:30.687
All right.


00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:32.690
I'm truly sorry
for your loss.


00:11:33.259 --> 00:11:34.624
Thank you.


00:13:02.782 --> 00:13:04.750
Oscar should only
have a quarter can


00:13:04.817 --> 00:13:06.148
morning and evening.


00:13:06.218 --> 00:13:07.776
And if you could
spend a little time


00:13:07.853 --> 00:13:09.946
with him every other day,
that'd be great.


00:13:10.022 --> 00:13:11.455
He loves people.


00:13:11.524 --> 00:13:13.492
I hope to be
back in a week.


00:13:13.559 --> 00:13:16.289
You know, Hank'll fire
you for real this time.


00:13:16.362 --> 00:13:18.489
Well, if he does,
it's his loss.


00:13:18.964 --> 00:13:20.625
Are you sure
you wanna do this?


00:13:20.699 --> 00:13:22.291
What would you
do if you were me?


00:13:22.368 --> 00:13:26.429
I trusted him and he used me.
I need to find out why.


00:13:35.915 --> 00:13:38.975
One of the conditions of the
house arrest was that Ron Osterberg


00:13:39.051 --> 00:13:43.044
hand over to Australia's
federal police and America's FBl


00:13:43.122 --> 00:13:46.683
all of the computer files and
documents requested in the court order.


00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:56.134
I will comment shortly.


00:13:56.202 --> 00:13:59.330
Abe, stay with the vehicle. Let's
go and get that computer inside.


00:14:06.712 --> 00:14:08.907
And now, one of the
world's financial giants


00:14:08.981 --> 00:14:11.142
forced to wear an ankle
bracelet like this one


00:14:11.217 --> 00:14:15.244
to ensure he never leaves his lavish
country estate without police escort.


00:14:15.321 --> 00:14:17.516
How have the
mighty fallen.


00:14:21.694 --> 00:14:23.855
Nice work, Inspector.


00:14:24.597 --> 00:14:28.328
You are gonna be burning
the midnight oil for months.


00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:29.833
Not me.


00:14:29.902 --> 00:14:32.496
That's what the forensic
accountants are for.


00:14:33.105 --> 00:14:35.096
I'm gonna nail
his ass for murder.


00:14:35.274 --> 00:14:37.242
You really think he had
Dennis Archer killed?


00:14:37.309 --> 00:14:39.971
He had the motive and the
resources to get it done.


00:14:40.045 --> 00:14:41.273
Be hard to prove,
won't it?


00:14:41.347 --> 00:14:44.407
A man like that usually
covers his tracks pretty well.


00:14:44.483 --> 00:14:46.383
Sooner or later,
he makes a mistake.


00:14:46.452 --> 00:14:49.216
When he does,
I'm gonna nail his ass.


00:14:54.159 --> 00:14:55.888
What I gave
them can't hurt me.


00:14:55.961 --> 00:14:57.622
They're wasting
their time.


00:14:57.696 --> 00:14:59.527
In a year or so, we'll
have a new government.


00:14:59.598 --> 00:15:02.192
I can promise you things
will be different then.


00:15:02.268 --> 00:15:05.635
We just have to hang in
there, stare the bastards down.


00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:12.702
FLIGHT ATTENDANT:
Ladies and gentlemen,


00:15:12.778 --> 00:15:14.769
we are now landing
at Coolangatta Airport.


00:15:14.847 --> 00:15:17.475
Enjoy your stay
on the Gold Coast.


00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:42.138
WOMAN OFFICER: Gold Coast police
station. How may I direct your call?


00:15:42.207 --> 00:15:44.266
Yes, Sergeant Smith...


00:15:44.343 --> 00:15:46.868
Yes, I'll put you
through to his voicemail.


00:15:46.946 --> 00:15:49.244
Excuse me,
I'd like to speak


00:15:49.315 --> 00:15:51.681
to the officer handling
the Archer case.


00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:52.876
Do you have
information on the case?


00:15:52.952 --> 00:15:53.976
Possibly.


00:15:54.053 --> 00:15:56.021
Your name?
Rebecca Scott.


00:15:56.088 --> 00:15:57.180
You American?


00:15:57.256 --> 00:15:58.280
Yes.


00:15:58.357 --> 00:16:00.120
Where from?
New York.


00:16:00.192 --> 00:16:03.252
Oh, wonderful city. I've
always wanted to go there.


00:16:03.329 --> 00:16:04.489
I will, when I
win the lottery.


00:16:05.397 --> 00:16:07.331
If you'd like to just
take a seat over there,


00:16:07.399 --> 00:16:09.299
I'll see if I can
find Inspector Hendricks.


00:16:10.903 --> 00:16:12.234
Inspector?


00:16:12.304 --> 00:16:16.138
I've just got someone
here about the Archer case.


00:16:16.208 --> 00:16:17.698
Okay.


00:16:35.094 --> 00:16:37.927
I've got $40 million...


00:16:37.997 --> 00:16:40.932
All right, here you go.


00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.126
...paper trail.


00:16:42.201 --> 00:16:45.693
If there's some way
we can connect these...


00:16:50.209 --> 00:16:52.404
You have information
about the Archer case?


00:16:52.478 --> 00:16:53.502
Not exactly.


00:16:53.579 --> 00:16:54.978
I'm a reporter
with Spyglass magazine


00:16:55.047 --> 00:16:56.378
in New York.
We're doing a story...


00:16:56.448 --> 00:16:57.881
You didn't tell me
she was a reporter.


00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.349
She failed to
mention it.


00:16:59.418 --> 00:17:01.352
This is an active
homicide investigation.


00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:02.682
We won't be releasing
any information


00:17:02.755 --> 00:17:04.154
to the media
until it's concluded.


00:17:04.223 --> 00:17:05.451
That's not
what I'm after.


00:17:05.524 --> 00:17:06.548
What is it that
you want then?


00:17:06.625 --> 00:17:08.786
I'm more interested
in a personal profile.


00:17:08.861 --> 00:17:11.625
What kind of man was Archer?
What was his life like here?


00:17:11.697 --> 00:17:13.255
That sort of thing. I'm
sorry, I can't help you.


00:17:13.332 --> 00:17:14.663
Maybe you could
give me the names


00:17:14.733 --> 00:17:16.200
of the people
who knew him best.


00:17:16.268 --> 00:17:17.963
Friends, coworkers...


00:17:18.037 --> 00:17:20.028
I'd love to
interview his wife.


00:17:20.105 --> 00:17:22.073
His wife?
Are you serious?


00:17:22.141 --> 00:17:23.768
Like I said, I'm
sorry, I can't help you.


00:17:23.842 --> 00:17:25.332
Excuse me.


00:18:11.757 --> 00:18:13.952
NELSON: Vassar
swim team, 2003.


00:18:14.026 --> 00:18:15.459
You've done
your homework.


00:18:15.527 --> 00:18:18.018
Your tax dollars
hard at work.


00:18:18.097 --> 00:18:20.998
You don't seem
surprised to see me.


00:18:21.066 --> 00:18:23.159
I had your passport
tagged for tracking.


00:18:24.837 --> 00:18:26.737
My tax dollars
hard at work.


00:18:26.805 --> 00:18:28.932
Exactly.


00:18:29.007 --> 00:18:31.999
Well, besides pissing
off the local cops,


00:18:32.077 --> 00:18:35.012
who I have to work
with, by the way,


00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.981
what do you intend on
accomplishing here, Mrs. Scott?


00:18:38.383 --> 00:18:40.010
Finding out the truth.


00:18:41.453 --> 00:18:44.013
Why don't you
let us handle that?


00:18:44.089 --> 00:18:46.250
How about this...


00:18:46.325 --> 00:18:49.192
Miles came to Sanctuary
Cove two years ago


00:18:49.261 --> 00:18:50.489
to work for Osterberg,


00:18:50.562 --> 00:18:52.553
not knowing that he
was a global criminal.


00:18:52.631 --> 00:18:54.030
And?


00:18:54.099 --> 00:18:55.794
Something went
really wrong,


00:18:55.868 --> 00:18:58.496
so Miles offered to
turn State's evidence.


00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:02.506
Osterberg had him
killed while you watched.


00:19:03.942 --> 00:19:05.341
Here's an idea.


00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:07.901
Why don't you go back to
New York and work on it?


00:19:08.147 --> 00:19:10.411
I wanna see my
husband's body.


00:19:10.482 --> 00:19:12.040
Well, you can't.


00:19:12.117 --> 00:19:13.106
Why not?


00:19:13.185 --> 00:19:14.277
Because we
can't find it.


00:19:14.353 --> 00:19:15.342
Excuse me?


00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:16.717
Well, we believe that,


00:19:16.788 --> 00:19:18.380
you know, the body was
dumped past the reef


00:19:18.457 --> 00:19:19.924
so the sharks
could feed off it.


00:19:19.992 --> 00:19:21.892
All we found
was his left pinky.


00:19:22.528 --> 00:19:24.519
I see.


00:19:24.596 --> 00:19:26.154
It's in a plastic
bag at the morgue


00:19:26.231 --> 00:19:28.096
if you wanna go
take a look at it.


00:19:37.743 --> 00:19:40.541
I'm sorry. I shouldn't
have said that.


00:19:46.885 --> 00:19:48.682
Look, if we're gonna
be working together,


00:19:48.754 --> 00:19:52.747
we should probably sit
down and share what we know.


00:19:52.824 --> 00:19:55.691
We're not gonna be working
together, Mrs. Scott.


00:19:55.761 --> 00:19:59.424
Fine. Then you go your
way, and I'll go mine.


00:20:01.033 --> 00:20:04.002
You lost your husband
twice. I get it.


00:20:04.069 --> 00:20:06.060
I lost a witness
I was supposed to protect.


00:20:06.138 --> 00:20:08.197
These are things
I cannot change.


00:20:08.273 --> 00:20:10.241
But I do have a job to do,


00:20:10.309 --> 00:20:13.710
and I don't have time to be
babysitting while I'm trying to do it.


00:20:13.779 --> 00:20:16.441
I can take care of
myself, thank you.


00:20:17.549 --> 00:20:21.144
I can have you arrested for
interfering with an investigation.


00:20:21.253 --> 00:20:23.221
Hmm.


00:20:23.288 --> 00:20:27.156
"FBl muzzles free press. "
Makes a good headline.


00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:34.394
Go home, Mrs. Scott.


00:20:36.168 --> 00:20:38.602
See you around.


00:21:33.825 --> 00:21:38.319
GPS.: In one kilometer, make a
left turn into Sanctuary Cove Road.


00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:30.814
Yes?


00:22:30.882 --> 00:22:32.247
Mrs. Archer?


00:22:32.317 --> 00:22:33.648
Yes.


00:22:34.252 --> 00:22:35.810
I'm Rebecca Scott.


00:22:35.887 --> 00:22:37.616
I'm with Spyglass
magazine in New York.


00:22:37.689 --> 00:22:39.623
Call my attorney.
No, please, please, please...


00:22:39.991 --> 00:22:41.083
Do you mind?


00:22:41.159 --> 00:22:42.524
We were married
to the same man.


00:22:43.829 --> 00:22:44.921
What?


00:22:44.996 --> 00:22:46.588
You knew him
as Dennis Archer,


00:22:46.898 --> 00:22:48.297
I knew him
as Miles Scott.


00:22:48.367 --> 00:22:49.800
We were married
for six years.


00:22:49.868 --> 00:22:51.358
You're joking.


00:22:51.436 --> 00:22:53.267
No, I'm not.


00:22:56.875 --> 00:22:58.274
Well, you'd better
come in then.


00:23:04.883 --> 00:23:06.817
Make yourself at home.


00:23:06.885 --> 00:23:09.718
Excuse the mess.
It's still not finished yet.


00:23:09.788 --> 00:23:11.153
It's beautiful.


00:23:11.223 --> 00:23:14.886
It's not bad. We only got
the place six months ago.


00:23:14.960 --> 00:23:17.986
Um... I was gonna make some
tea. Would you like some?


00:23:18.063 --> 00:23:19.621
Yes, that would
be lovely.


00:23:21.433 --> 00:23:22.957
BRIGlD: Lemon or honey?


00:23:23.034 --> 00:23:24.524
Lemon.


00:23:49.795 --> 00:23:52.958
So, Dennis'
first wife.


00:23:54.166 --> 00:23:56.464
He never mentioned that
he was married before.


00:23:56.535 --> 00:23:57.797
When did you divorce?


00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:00.504
We didn't.


00:24:04.943 --> 00:24:06.968
Do you have a photo
or something of Dennis?


00:24:07.045 --> 00:24:08.637
Just so I can...


00:24:08.713 --> 00:24:10.806
Of course, absolutely.


00:24:14.019 --> 00:24:15.953
Miles Scott, my husband,


00:24:16.021 --> 00:24:18.182
died two years ago in
a car crash in New York,


00:24:18.457 --> 00:24:21.187
burned beyond recognition,


00:24:21.259 --> 00:24:23.921
or so I believed.


00:24:23.995 --> 00:24:28.227
Now I learn that he's been
living here as Dennis Archer.


00:24:30.335 --> 00:24:31.927
The police never
mentioned anything.


00:24:32.003 --> 00:24:33.197
The FBl told me.


00:24:33.271 --> 00:24:35.501
FBl?


00:24:35.574 --> 00:24:38.771
An American guy
came to see me.


00:24:38.844 --> 00:24:40.368
I had no idea.


00:24:41.112 --> 00:24:43.478
No, neither did I.


00:24:44.683 --> 00:24:45.672
Mmm.


00:24:47.452 --> 00:24:49.113
Was Miles...


00:24:49.187 --> 00:24:51.917
Dennis.
Was Dennis good to you?


00:24:52.424 --> 00:24:54.688
Of course.


00:24:54.759 --> 00:24:56.158
He loved me.


00:24:56.962 --> 00:25:00.022
He bought me nice things,
took me nice places,


00:25:00.098 --> 00:25:02.532
and he was always
hot for it.


00:25:02.601 --> 00:25:05.968
But I'm sure you
remember that, don't you?


00:25:10.375 --> 00:25:11.774
Did...


00:25:12.544 --> 00:25:16.537
Was Dennis having trouble
at work before he...


00:25:17.382 --> 00:25:19.714
Not that I know of.


00:25:19.784 --> 00:25:25.051
Can I ask you, did he leave
you well taken care of?


00:25:25.123 --> 00:25:28.217
I mean, the first time
that he died.


00:25:29.127 --> 00:25:30.719
Not particularly.


00:25:32.597 --> 00:25:34.155
That sucks.


00:25:34.666 --> 00:25:37.430
I'm getting everything.


00:25:37.502 --> 00:25:40.062
You're not here to claim
on the estate, or...


00:25:40.138 --> 00:25:42.902
Did Dennis ever mention
a man named Osterberg?


00:25:43.775 --> 00:25:45.037
Who?


00:25:45.110 --> 00:25:47.271
Dennis worked for him.


00:25:47.345 --> 00:25:49.575
Dennis never mentioned
anything about work.


00:25:49.648 --> 00:25:52.947
Ronald Osterberg, he's been
indicted for major embezzlement.


00:25:53.018 --> 00:25:55.578
That's right. Wasn't it
on the news or something?


00:25:55.654 --> 00:25:57.315
Yeah, it was.


00:25:57.389 --> 00:26:01.689
My husband had nothing to do
with this Osterberg character.


00:26:01.760 --> 00:26:05.161
I'm not looking to ruin
your reputation, Mrs. Archer.


00:26:05.230 --> 00:26:07.130
I'm just looking
for some answers.


00:26:07.198 --> 00:26:08.927
Well, I'm afraid
I can't help you.


00:26:10.468 --> 00:26:13.266
Everybody I know
loved Dennis.


00:26:13.338 --> 00:26:15.738
No one would've
wanted him dead.


00:26:17.375 --> 00:26:20.936
I don't know what
I'm gonna do without him.


00:26:21.346 --> 00:26:23.439
I'm sorry if
I've upset you.


00:26:23.515 --> 00:26:26.973
Yeah, well,
you have, actually.


00:26:27.953 --> 00:26:29.648
I think it's time
you should go.


00:26:29.721 --> 00:26:33.157
I have things to attend
to, a memorial to organize.


00:26:33.224 --> 00:26:35.556
Of course, you're more
than welcome to come.


00:26:35.627 --> 00:26:36.651
Of course.


00:26:36.795 --> 00:26:37.853
Yeah.


00:26:43.969 --> 00:26:45.800
I'm sorry for your loss.


00:26:47.439 --> 00:26:49.031
And you for yours.


00:30:05.870 --> 00:30:09.363
Call the police!


00:30:32.130 --> 00:30:33.893
NELSON: She's uploading
her photos now.


00:30:34.132 --> 00:30:36.692
Run the plates and let's
track this guy down.


00:30:38.403 --> 00:30:41.634
So you dropped by
Brigid Archer's house.


00:30:41.706 --> 00:30:43.196
She called the police.


00:30:43.274 --> 00:30:44.332
I must've
frightened her.


00:30:44.409 --> 00:30:45.398
Yeah.


00:30:45.476 --> 00:30:47.341
What did you
make of her?


00:30:47.412 --> 00:30:49.209
Trophy wife.


00:30:49.280 --> 00:30:52.716
Her bereavement seemed more like
a bad hangover than a tragedy,


00:30:52.784 --> 00:30:54.342
but she's not a suspect.


00:30:54.419 --> 00:30:57.286
I don't know. Something about
her just didn't feel right.


00:30:59.724 --> 00:31:01.487
Her husband
is murdered.


00:31:01.559 --> 00:31:03.925
His other wife who she
didn't even know existed


00:31:03.995 --> 00:31:05.656
until you paid her a visit,


00:31:05.730 --> 00:31:07.254
shows up at her
house uninvited.


00:31:07.332 --> 00:31:08.560
Now, how would you act?
No...


00:31:08.633 --> 00:31:11.466
Yes, I get all of
that, but still,


00:31:11.536 --> 00:31:14.801
it was like she was
hiding something.


00:31:14.873 --> 00:31:17.865
So she hires hitmen
to kill her husband?


00:31:17.942 --> 00:31:19.534
I doubt that.


00:31:19.611 --> 00:31:21.306
Osterberg, he's
capable of anything.


00:31:21.379 --> 00:31:22.869
Ah, Osterberg!


00:31:22.947 --> 00:31:25.211
So Osterberg hires somebody
to run you off the road?


00:31:25.283 --> 00:31:26.307
Possibly.


00:31:26.384 --> 00:31:28.648
All right, I'll bite.
Why?


00:31:28.720 --> 00:31:32.588
I'm digging around.
Maybe I'll turn up something.


00:31:32.657 --> 00:31:34.557
I do have a reputation
for that sort of thing.


00:31:34.626 --> 00:31:36.287
Oh, yeah, your reputation, of course.


00:31:37.629 --> 00:31:38.926
Know what I think?


00:31:38.997 --> 00:31:41.591
I think you cut somebody off, and
they were just returning the favor.


00:31:41.666 --> 00:31:43.224
We'll see.


00:31:43.401 --> 00:31:44.732
Nelson.


00:31:46.237 --> 00:31:48.535
No, no, I'm gonna stop
by his yacht tomorrow,


00:31:48.606 --> 00:31:50.198
make sure we
didn't miss anything.


00:31:50.508 --> 00:31:51.600
Thanks.


00:31:51.676 --> 00:31:53.610
I'm coming with
you to the yacht.


00:31:53.678 --> 00:31:56.272
And people in hell
want ice water.


00:31:58.016 --> 00:32:00.951
Listen, enjoy the hotel.


00:32:01.019 --> 00:32:02.213
You're on vacation.


00:32:02.587 --> 00:32:04.817
I just booked
your flight.


00:32:09.661 --> 00:32:13.927
OSTERBERG: As you all know, we've
invested over $4.5 billion worldwide.


00:32:13.998 --> 00:32:17.331
We've created over 2,000 jobs
in northern America alone,


00:32:17.402 --> 00:32:18.528
and over the next
five years,


00:32:18.636 --> 00:32:22.003
we intend to invest another
$5 billion in Australia.


00:32:22.073 --> 00:32:25.600
Now, of course, we're encountering
problems with this government.


00:34:30.701 --> 00:34:32.100
Hello?


00:34:32.737 --> 00:34:34.500
Anybody there?


00:34:37.341 --> 00:34:38.899
Hello?


00:35:16.848 --> 00:35:18.748
REBECCA: Surprise.


00:35:19.183 --> 00:35:20.844
But is it really?


00:35:20.918 --> 00:35:22.886
What have you
got to lose?


00:35:23.054 --> 00:35:24.043
I wanna see
the boat.


00:35:25.456 --> 00:35:29.256
Or I could handcuff you
to that post right there.


00:35:32.196 --> 00:35:34.096
You coming?


00:35:35.967 --> 00:35:38.060
So what'd you
turn up on my husband


00:35:38.136 --> 00:35:40.661
before he became
Dennis Archer?


00:35:40.738 --> 00:35:42.035
Quite a bit.


00:35:42.106 --> 00:35:43.733
Tell me.


00:35:43.841 --> 00:35:45.468
I don't think
that's a good idea.


00:35:45.543 --> 00:35:49.570
I have a right to know,
especially under the circumstances.


00:35:49.647 --> 00:35:51.672
Well, it appears
your Miles Scott


00:35:51.782 --> 00:35:56.276
was a mild-mannered, squeaky-clean
tax accountant by day,


00:35:56.354 --> 00:35:58.686
and a serial swindler
in his spare time.


00:35:58.890 --> 00:36:01.859
Dabbled in Ponzi schemes,
money laundering,


00:36:01.926 --> 00:36:03.416
hell, even fake charities.


00:36:03.494 --> 00:36:05.758
That's impossible.
I would've known.


00:36:05.830 --> 00:36:09.027
No, you wouldn't have
'cause he was that good.


00:36:09.100 --> 00:36:12.695
Always traveled in the
shadows, a Teflon grifter.


00:36:12.770 --> 00:36:15.603
Nothing ever stuck to the man
except other people's money.


00:36:15.673 --> 00:36:17.538
Oh, boy.


00:36:17.608 --> 00:36:19.667
Told you you
didn't wanna hear it.


00:36:19.744 --> 00:36:22.178
But you were right about
his connection to Osterberg.


00:36:22.246 --> 00:36:24.714
They were involved
in the same Ponzi scheme.


00:36:24.782 --> 00:36:26.374
Your husband's
work impressed him,


00:36:26.450 --> 00:36:27.508
so he brought
him down here


00:36:27.585 --> 00:36:30.076
to be his man behind
the scenes, so to speak.


00:36:30.221 --> 00:36:31.984
Routing money through a
string of shell companies


00:36:32.056 --> 00:36:33.887
until it vanished
without a trace.


00:36:33.958 --> 00:36:37.052
But he didn't need
to fake his own death.


00:36:37.128 --> 00:36:41.588
It was either that or get rid of
you. Couldn't scam you forever.


00:36:41.666 --> 00:36:45.466
He wouldn't have
done that, not to me.


00:36:45.536 --> 00:36:46.935
You really think so?


00:36:47.004 --> 00:36:49.802
A man that faked
his own death?


00:36:55.680 --> 00:36:59.081
Money makes a man's
moral compass go haywire.


00:36:59.150 --> 00:37:03.177
Everything was fine until
Osterberg got indicted in the US.


00:37:03.621 --> 00:37:08.183
At our request, the Australian federal
police put him under house arrest.


00:37:08.259 --> 00:37:09.954
Dennis feared
that he'd be next.


00:37:10.027 --> 00:37:13.087
So he offered to turn
State's evidence.


00:37:13.497 --> 00:37:16.227
Called me and said
he had what I needed.


00:37:16.300 --> 00:37:19.758
I came down here to pick
him up, and they killed him.


00:37:24.308 --> 00:37:25.297
Wow.


00:37:26.244 --> 00:37:30.840
Yeah, they say you can tell a man's
insecurity by the size of his boat.


00:37:32.917 --> 00:37:34.748
What is it?


00:37:35.286 --> 00:37:38.312
Miles loved boats.


00:37:38.389 --> 00:37:43.190
One year for his birthday, I
had a model yacht made for him.


00:37:43.261 --> 00:37:47.561
Even had the maker put
Dreamboat on the side of it.


00:37:47.965 --> 00:37:49.694
Sure is a beautiful boat.


00:37:49.900 --> 00:37:51.424
Yeah, it is.


00:38:02.013 --> 00:38:03.446
Go back,
call the police.


00:38:03.514 --> 00:38:05.277
You sure?
Do it.


00:38:28.539 --> 00:38:30.166
Come on.


00:38:31.008 --> 00:38:32.771
OFFICER: Gold Coast Police.
How can I help you?


00:38:32.843 --> 00:38:36.006
This is Rebecca Scott. I'm with
FBl Agent Nelson down at the...


00:38:36.080 --> 00:38:37.104
OFFICER: Please hold.


00:39:18.689 --> 00:39:20.418
Come on.


00:39:51.155 --> 00:39:52.213
OFFICER: What's
your emergency?


00:39:52.323 --> 00:39:54.883
Send the police to
Sanctuary Cove Marina now.


00:39:54.959 --> 00:39:57.018
Stay on the line.


00:41:03.928 --> 00:41:05.293
Damn it.


00:41:31.589 --> 00:41:32.817
The cops are coming!


00:41:33.791 --> 00:41:34.985
THUG: We gotta go now!


00:41:35.893 --> 00:41:37.190
Move it!


00:42:06.724 --> 00:42:07.850
You all right?


00:42:08.158 --> 00:42:09.360
Yeah.


00:42:13.397 --> 00:42:15.058
Okay, come on.


00:42:17.101 --> 00:42:18.534
OFFICER: Can you describe
the man, Mrs. Scott?


00:42:18.602 --> 00:42:20.069
About 5'9".
Okay.


00:42:20.137 --> 00:42:23.698
Light brown hair, scruffy
beard, 30 years old.


00:42:23.774 --> 00:42:25.503
I'd recognize him
if I saw him again.


00:42:25.576 --> 00:42:27.407
Thanks.


00:42:28.212 --> 00:42:31.113
Anything on
that plate?


00:42:31.181 --> 00:42:32.170
How you feeling?


00:42:32.249 --> 00:42:33.341
I'm fine.


00:42:34.318 --> 00:42:35.910
A word?


00:42:37.021 --> 00:42:38.818
I have concerns
about the continual


00:42:38.889 --> 00:42:42.347
presence of Mrs. Scott
on this investigation.


00:42:42.426 --> 00:42:45.293
The FBl, and certainly my
superiors at the federal police,


00:42:45.362 --> 00:42:48.729
would be quite displeased with both
of us if this case is compromised


00:42:48.799 --> 00:42:50.232
because confidential
information ends up


00:42:50.301 --> 00:42:51.666
on the front page
of some newspaper.


00:42:51.769 --> 00:42:54.397
Someone keeps
trying to kill her.


00:42:54.471 --> 00:42:56.098
I'm not about to
lose another witness.


00:42:56.173 --> 00:42:57.470
Now, she plays
a part in all this,


00:42:57.541 --> 00:42:58.906
and I'm gonna find
out what that part is.


00:42:58.976 --> 00:43:00.204
Anybody that has
a problem with that,


00:43:00.277 --> 00:43:01.744
they can contact
my supervisor.


00:43:01.812 --> 00:43:03.712
Until then,
this is my investigation,


00:43:03.781 --> 00:43:05.612
and I will run
it how I see fit.


00:43:05.683 --> 00:43:07.674
Okay, that's fine.


00:43:07.751 --> 00:43:11.209
But if she screws this up for
everybody, it's your ass, not mine.


00:43:11.288 --> 00:43:12.585
Agreed?


00:43:12.656 --> 00:43:13.918
Never doubted it.


00:43:15.326 --> 00:43:16.588
Now how about
that plate?


00:43:16.660 --> 00:43:17.888
Yeah.


00:43:19.129 --> 00:43:22.326
We traced the vehicle to a subsidiary
company of the Osterberg group.


00:43:22.399 --> 00:43:24.264
Reported missing
about a week ago.


00:43:24.335 --> 00:43:26.428
Naturally. The question is


00:43:26.503 --> 00:43:29.165
were they trying to
scare off a pesky reporter


00:43:29.740 --> 00:43:31.970
or did they mean
to do her serious harm?


00:43:32.042 --> 00:43:33.202
You tell me.


00:43:34.712 --> 00:43:36.942
That guy on the boat was
looking for something,


00:43:37.014 --> 00:43:39.414
and what that something
is, I have no idea.


00:43:39.483 --> 00:43:43.112
I mean, they had to have searched
it before they killed Archer.


00:43:43.187 --> 00:43:44.245
Want me to
take a look?


00:43:44.388 --> 00:43:45.480
No.


00:43:45.556 --> 00:43:48.753
Agent Nelson, I knew him much
better than either of you.


00:43:50.995 --> 00:43:52.485
This is true.


00:43:52.563 --> 00:43:54.827
All right, look,
that's your call.


00:43:54.898 --> 00:43:57.264
I don't want anything to do with this.


00:44:05.309 --> 00:44:08.244
NELSON: We've searched
every part of this ship,


00:44:08.312 --> 00:44:10.746
and now we're
in the engine room.


00:44:10.948 --> 00:44:13.178
Please tell me you're
not wasting our time.


00:44:13.250 --> 00:44:15.718
Yeah.


00:44:20.224 --> 00:44:23.091
You know,
you probably saved my life.


00:44:23.160 --> 00:44:25.128
I'm sure it won't
be the last time.


00:44:26.030 --> 00:44:27.520
I'm starting to like you.


00:44:27.598 --> 00:44:28.690
Oh, God forbid.


00:44:28.766 --> 00:44:29.790
Ah, just a little bit.


00:44:31.101 --> 00:44:33.661
You're not the usual fed
with a stick up his ass.


00:44:33.737 --> 00:44:35.830
I'm sure that fell
out when I got attacked.


00:44:38.442 --> 00:44:39.932
After you.


00:44:49.753 --> 00:44:51.380
That ain't good.


00:45:18.649 --> 00:45:20.913
Why would he
blow up the boat?


00:45:20.984 --> 00:45:23.578
To destroy any evidence
Archer left behind.


00:45:25.422 --> 00:45:28.186
So you think Osterberg
is running scared now?


00:45:28.258 --> 00:45:30.021
If he isn't,
he soon will be.


00:45:51.248 --> 00:45:52.408
Go ahead.


00:46:07.631 --> 00:46:08.620
Ah.


00:46:08.899 --> 00:46:10.696
Agent Nelson.


00:46:11.101 --> 00:46:13.661
And you must be
Rebecca Scott.


00:46:13.737 --> 00:46:15.671
Your husband
spoke of you often.


00:46:15.739 --> 00:46:17.798
May I call you Rebecca?


00:46:17.875 --> 00:46:19.399
Screw you.


00:46:19.476 --> 00:46:21.569
I'll take that as a yes.


00:46:21.645 --> 00:46:23.374
Consider this a warning.


00:46:23.447 --> 00:46:25.813
Really? What about?


00:46:25.883 --> 00:46:27.748
What'll happen
if you don't back off.


00:46:27.818 --> 00:46:30.252
I'm sure I don't know
what you're talking about.


00:46:30.320 --> 00:46:33.016
We were on that yacht today
right before it exploded.


00:46:33.223 --> 00:46:38.058
Whose yacht are we talking
about? Not mine, I hope.


00:46:38.128 --> 00:46:41.063
You think you're safe in
here? No one can get to you?


00:46:41.131 --> 00:46:43.156
I'll ignore the threatening
tone in the hope


00:46:43.233 --> 00:46:45.292
that we can have
a civilized conversation.


00:46:45.936 --> 00:46:49.303
So I assume Dennis
Archer's boat was destroyed


00:46:49.373 --> 00:46:51.500
and you think
that I'm responsible?


00:46:51.575 --> 00:46:53.338
You killed my husband.


00:46:53.410 --> 00:46:54.934
Why would I do that?


00:46:55.012 --> 00:46:56.536
He was about to
inform on you.


00:46:57.047 --> 00:47:00.107
I don't kill people,
Rebecca, I buy them.


00:47:00.184 --> 00:47:02.345
Not everybody has a price.


00:47:02.920 --> 00:47:04.854
I beg to differ.


00:47:04.922 --> 00:47:07.015
I was rather fond
of your husband.


00:47:07.090 --> 00:47:08.785
We worked well together.


00:47:08.859 --> 00:47:10.986
Though, he was
a little light-fingered.


00:47:11.094 --> 00:47:12.789
You two were a lot
alike, apparently.


00:47:12.896 --> 00:47:14.659
You knew he was
stealing from you?


00:47:14.731 --> 00:47:16.824
More like petty cash.


00:47:17.334 --> 00:47:20.531
I tolerated it because he was
good at what I needed him for.


00:47:20.604 --> 00:47:21.696
Which was?


00:47:21.772 --> 00:47:22.966
I'm sorry.


00:47:23.040 --> 00:47:25.235
I'm forbidden to discuss
my business matters


00:47:25.309 --> 00:47:27.436
until I come
before the courts.


00:47:27.744 --> 00:47:31.510
And that will be a very long
time in the future, if at all.


00:47:31.949 --> 00:47:34.577
Until then,
I'm very comfortable here.


00:47:34.651 --> 00:47:35.913
Oh, don't get used to it.


00:47:36.286 --> 00:47:39.847
You'll be trading this view
for an 8 x 10 cell soon enough.


00:47:39.923 --> 00:47:43.689
You're making predictions way
above your pay grade, Agent Nelson.


00:47:43.760 --> 00:47:45.523
Do you really think that
the Australian government


00:47:45.596 --> 00:47:47.530
will allow me
to be extradited?


00:47:47.598 --> 00:47:49.463
I'm not some
embarrassing whistleblower


00:47:49.533 --> 00:47:51.524
who's been caught
with his pants down.


00:47:51.602 --> 00:47:53.832
I'm a multinational
corporation.


00:47:53.904 --> 00:47:56.372
I've created
thousands ofjobs,


00:47:56.473 --> 00:47:59.203
made major investments
in mining and tourism.


00:47:59.276 --> 00:48:03.838
These matters will be settled between
governments behind closed doors


00:48:03.914 --> 00:48:05.472
as they always have been.


00:48:05.949 --> 00:48:07.814
Would you care
to stay for lunch?


00:48:08.619 --> 00:48:10.382
I'd care to kick your ass.


00:48:10.520 --> 00:48:11.680
Ooh.


00:48:30.140 --> 00:48:32.040
How about some lunch?


00:48:32.776 --> 00:48:36.075
Glass of wine,
a little timeout.


00:48:36.480 --> 00:48:37.845
Yeah.


00:48:46.623 --> 00:48:49.956
I spent four years of my life
trying to bring this guy down.


00:48:50.027 --> 00:48:52.427
He's a mega crook
like Osterberg,


00:48:52.496 --> 00:48:54.555
buying into companies
and looting them


00:48:54.631 --> 00:48:57.532
until there was nothing left
and then moving on.


00:48:57.634 --> 00:48:59.602
I was obsessed.
Did you get him?


00:49:00.170 --> 00:49:03.606
I had enough evidence to put
him away for about 100 years.


00:49:04.007 --> 00:49:05.133
And?


00:49:05.809 --> 00:49:08.073
Walked on a technicality.
Oh!


00:49:08.712 --> 00:49:12.239
That's terrible.
All that work for nothing.


00:49:12.316 --> 00:49:14.250
I still got promoted.
Great.


00:49:14.318 --> 00:49:15.649
And then my wife left me.


00:49:15.719 --> 00:49:18.244
Not so great.
How come?


00:49:18.322 --> 00:49:22.554
You know, I was all about the
work. She came in a distant second.


00:49:22.626 --> 00:49:24.651
Who's gonna
put up with that?


00:49:27.431 --> 00:49:30.161
You still wear
your ring.


00:49:30.934 --> 00:49:33.494
Old habits die hard,
I guess.


00:49:35.906 --> 00:49:38.932
Yeah, work's
a great healer.


00:49:40.310 --> 00:49:43.541
Take my advice, young lady.
Live a little.


00:49:44.982 --> 00:49:46.574
It goes fast.


00:49:46.650 --> 00:49:49.448
Maybe I will,
after all this is settled.


00:49:53.490 --> 00:49:57.256
You went through my husband's
office, his computers?


00:49:57.361 --> 00:49:58.851
Yeah, nothing there.


00:49:58.929 --> 00:50:00.396
You wiped his hard drives?


00:50:00.464 --> 00:50:02.329
No, but it's just
all the normal stuff.


00:50:02.666 --> 00:50:04.327
How do you mean?


00:50:04.401 --> 00:50:07.165
Well, a guy like him,
a grifter, an embezzler,


00:50:07.237 --> 00:50:08.670
you'd expect
to find something.


00:50:08.739 --> 00:50:09.967
Like what?


00:50:10.040 --> 00:50:13.874
Something out of place.
Nope, all by the books.


00:50:14.811 --> 00:50:16.301
Interesting.


00:50:17.447 --> 00:50:19.472
Don't even think about it.


00:50:19.549 --> 00:50:21.039
What?
What?


00:50:21.118 --> 00:50:25.179
What? Going by there. Besides,
we already cleaned it all out.


00:50:25.255 --> 00:50:28.452
I would never interfere
with your work, Agent Nelson.


00:50:28.525 --> 00:50:30.652
No, I noticed. Yeah.


00:50:31.128 --> 00:50:32.459
Here you go.


00:50:32.529 --> 00:50:34.360
How much do I owe?


00:50:35.065 --> 00:50:36.794
All of it.
What?


00:50:36.867 --> 00:50:38.357
Your magazine has
an expense account.


00:50:38.502 --> 00:50:40.026
So do you.


00:50:40.103 --> 00:50:42.094
I work for the
US government, girl.


00:50:42.172 --> 00:50:44.606
$17 trillion in deficit.


00:50:44.674 --> 00:50:47.006
You don't wanna
add to that, do you?


00:50:47.077 --> 00:50:48.237
Unbelievable.


00:50:48.378 --> 00:50:50.710
Where's your
sense of patriotism?


00:51:19.409 --> 00:51:21.206
THUG 1: Power's cut?
THUG 2: Yes, mate.


00:51:21.278 --> 00:51:22.802
THUG 1: What about the alarm?
THUG 2: Yeah.


00:52:15.732 --> 00:52:17.757
Help.


00:52:38.188 --> 00:52:39.712
THUG: Give it up. Shut up.


00:52:40.223 --> 00:52:43.317
BRIGlD: Please.
I did everything he asked.


00:52:44.661 --> 00:52:48.028
No! No! No!


00:52:49.032 --> 00:52:51.227
No! No!


00:53:51.828 --> 00:53:55.320
REBECCA: This is Rebecca.
Please leave a message.


00:55:10.073 --> 00:55:11.836
Just have a few more
things to check out but


00:55:11.908 --> 00:55:13.603
you'll have my report
by the end of the week.


00:55:13.677 --> 00:55:14.803
MAN: I'm counting on it.


00:55:14.878 --> 00:55:16.140
Yes, sir.


00:55:16.212 --> 00:55:17.577
Thank you, sir.


00:55:20.317 --> 00:55:22.877
You went to
see Osterberg.


00:55:22.952 --> 00:55:24.044
I did.


00:55:24.120 --> 00:55:26.213
Without telling me.


00:55:26.323 --> 00:55:28.553
Oh, it was a
personal visit.


00:55:28.625 --> 00:55:29.887
Really?


00:55:29.959 --> 00:55:31.620
Was it personal when you
went to collect Archer


00:55:31.695 --> 00:55:33.026
without calling me
for back up?


00:55:33.096 --> 00:55:35.360
No, that was my bad.


00:55:35.432 --> 00:55:36.558
And now he's dead.


00:55:36.633 --> 00:55:38.225
And you are still
letting this reporter


00:55:38.301 --> 00:55:40.030
stick her nose
into everything we do.


00:55:40.103 --> 00:55:41.661
Brother,
it's like I said,


00:55:41.738 --> 00:55:43.262
she became a part
of this investigation


00:55:43.340 --> 00:55:44.807
the moment they
tried to kill her.


00:55:44.874 --> 00:55:48.207
As far as I'm concerned, your
judgment can't be trusted.


00:55:48.745 --> 00:55:50.736
And for the record,
I'll no longer be sharing


00:55:50.814 --> 00:55:52.679
any information with
you or your bureau.


00:55:52.749 --> 00:55:54.011
Is that right?


00:55:54.084 --> 00:55:55.449
And if you've got
a problem with that,


00:55:55.518 --> 00:55:57.179
feel free to
contact Washington,


00:55:57.253 --> 00:55:59.687
and I'll be happy
to give them my reasons.


00:56:01.524 --> 00:56:04.049
You're a hell of a
conversationalist, Hendricks.


00:56:04.127 --> 00:56:05.856
Just stay out of my way.


00:56:05.929 --> 00:56:07.794
Nice talking to you.


00:56:25.482 --> 00:56:28.383
DELIVERY MAN: Mate, can you tell me
where Dreamboat Financial Services is?


00:56:28.451 --> 00:56:30.612
CONCIERGE: Dreamboat.
Third level, 309.


00:56:30.687 --> 00:56:32.348
DELIVERY MAN: Thank you.


00:56:52.375 --> 00:56:53.672
Delivery.


00:56:54.344 --> 00:56:56.175
Hi, can I help you?


00:56:56.246 --> 00:56:58.043
Package for...
Dreamboat?


00:56:58.114 --> 00:56:59.877
Yeah.
Great.


00:56:59.949 --> 00:57:01.382
Sign here.


00:57:03.787 --> 00:57:05.448
Thanks.


00:57:48.064 --> 00:57:49.429
Free sample.


00:58:32.041 --> 00:58:34.339
Come on, answer
your damn phone, girl.


00:58:34.410 --> 00:58:37.777
REBECCA: This is Rebecca.
Please leave a message.


00:58:43.319 --> 00:58:45.287
My birthday.


00:58:45.355 --> 00:58:48.483
Oh, Miles, you remembered.


00:59:00.737 --> 00:59:02.034
Wow.


00:59:02.105 --> 00:59:04.039
The money's just rolling in.


00:59:04.107 --> 00:59:06.769
Miles, what were
you guys doing?


00:59:06.843 --> 00:59:08.538
$2 million.


00:59:08.978 --> 00:59:10.445
Hmm.


00:59:10.680 --> 00:59:11.874
Here.


00:59:11.948 --> 00:59:14.678
Maybe you put it in here.


00:59:16.452 --> 00:59:18.352
Cash transfer?


00:59:19.289 --> 00:59:21.018
$4 million?


00:59:21.090 --> 00:59:23.058
Where?


00:59:23.126 --> 00:59:26.527
Okay. Here we go.


00:59:31.167 --> 00:59:33.294
No, no, no, no, no.


00:59:33.870 --> 00:59:35.167
Shoot.


00:59:59.963 --> 01:00:01.487
I'll take the back.


01:01:02.825 --> 01:01:05.293
Help! Help!


01:01:05.361 --> 01:01:07.158
Let go of me!


01:01:07.230 --> 01:01:08.993
Help!


01:01:22.011 --> 01:01:23.205
Oh, my God.


01:01:23.279 --> 01:01:25.213
You all right, mate?


01:01:25.281 --> 01:01:26.373
WOMAN: Someone
call Triple Zero.


01:01:26.449 --> 01:01:27.609
Oh, my God.


01:01:34.724 --> 01:01:36.885
Thank you.
I'll take it from here.


01:01:42.465 --> 01:01:43.591
You all right?


01:01:43.666 --> 01:01:45.497
Yeah, I'm good.


01:01:50.106 --> 01:01:52.768
You mind telling me where
you went this morning?


01:01:54.110 --> 01:01:56.544
I had a look at
my husband's office.


01:01:56.879 --> 01:01:58.870
After I told you there
was nothing there?


01:01:58.948 --> 01:02:00.745
His other office.


01:02:00.850 --> 01:02:02.374
What other office?


01:02:02.452 --> 01:02:04.352
He had another office
on the same floor.


01:02:05.588 --> 01:02:06.577
Huh.


01:02:07.123 --> 01:02:08.249
How'd you find it?


01:02:08.324 --> 01:02:10.622
Remember the name
of my husband's boat?


01:02:10.693 --> 01:02:11.717
Dreamboat.


01:02:11.794 --> 01:02:15.093
Dreamboat Financial Services,
third floor east.


01:02:15.164 --> 01:02:17.689
Nothing in it but a
refrigerator and a computer.


01:02:17.767 --> 01:02:19.098
And?


01:02:20.036 --> 01:02:24.166
He was siphoning money out
of Osterberg's accounts.


01:02:24.707 --> 01:02:26.607
Almost $10 million.


01:02:27.744 --> 01:02:28.733
Whoo!


01:02:29.045 --> 01:02:30.444
Well, what'd
he do with it?


01:02:30.513 --> 01:02:32.708
Cashed out,
probably hid it somewhere.


01:02:33.983 --> 01:02:36.781
Huh. No wonder Osterberg
wanted him whacked.


01:02:36.853 --> 01:02:38.445
It doesn't make sense.


01:02:38.521 --> 01:02:39.510
What?


01:02:39.589 --> 01:02:42.183
Would you kill someone that had
$10 million that belonged to you?


01:02:42.258 --> 01:02:45.591
Not till I got it back.
I'd do damage to the boy.


01:02:46.195 --> 01:02:48.425
I want you on a plane
back to New York today.


01:02:48.498 --> 01:02:49.795
Hey, chill out.


01:02:49.866 --> 01:02:52.232
She has no business
interfering in this case.


01:02:52.301 --> 01:02:53.461
That man tried
to kill me.


01:02:53.536 --> 01:02:55.527
The same man
I saw at the marina.


01:02:55.605 --> 01:02:58.165
Christopher Del Flannery,
robbery with violence,


01:02:58.241 --> 01:03:00.038
suspect in two
contract killings,


01:03:00.109 --> 01:03:02.805
worked as a security guard for
one of Osterberg's companies,


01:03:02.879 --> 01:03:04.312
dismissed three weeks ago.


01:03:04.380 --> 01:03:08.111
We were that close to nailing
the guy, but he's dead.


01:03:08.184 --> 01:03:09.981
Could've been a
goldmine of information.


01:03:10.052 --> 01:03:11.076
Inspector.


01:03:11.154 --> 01:03:12.143
Not now.


01:03:12.221 --> 01:03:14.018
OFFICER: There's been
another homicide.


01:03:14.090 --> 01:03:15.580
Brigid Archer.


01:03:30.072 --> 01:03:32.540
Can I see some
identification please?


01:03:32.608 --> 01:03:35.042
She's with me.


01:03:48.324 --> 01:03:49.518
Watch your back there.


01:03:57.366 --> 01:03:59.197
Wait here.


01:04:02.205 --> 01:04:03.570
Get her outta here.


01:04:03.639 --> 01:04:04.731
She stays.


01:04:04.807 --> 01:04:06.832
I'm just keeping an eye
on her, like you asked.


01:04:06.909 --> 01:04:08.376
Strictly speaking,
this is not a crime


01:04:08.444 --> 01:04:10.036
over which you
have any jurisdiction.


01:04:11.280 --> 01:04:12.747
Humor me.


01:04:15.017 --> 01:04:17.076
The alarm's been fried,


01:04:17.153 --> 01:04:20.088
signs of forced entry on
the door into the pool area.


01:04:20.456 --> 01:04:22.890
Now, footprints indicate
there was two of them.


01:04:22.959 --> 01:04:25.018
Now, my guess
is she's heard a noise,


01:04:25.094 --> 01:04:26.959
come down to investigate,
then drowned.


01:04:27.029 --> 01:04:28.553
Then they ransacked the place.


01:04:28.631 --> 01:04:29.655
Anything stolen?


01:04:29.732 --> 01:04:31.131
Doesn't look like it.


01:04:31.200 --> 01:04:34.135
Trying to track down the
housekeeper, see what she can tell us.


01:04:34.203 --> 01:04:35.795
But I think we both
know who's behind this.


01:04:37.340 --> 01:04:38.898
Mind if I have
a look around?


01:04:38.975 --> 01:04:40.499
Yes, I do.


01:04:40.576 --> 01:04:42.544
But I'm too busy to
make an issue out of it.


01:04:42.612 --> 01:04:43.636
We're dusting
for prints,


01:04:43.713 --> 01:04:46.876
so make sure Lois Lane there
doesn't contaminate the crime scene.


01:04:52.388 --> 01:04:54.788
Does that make
me Superman?


01:04:59.996 --> 01:05:03.830
You think this guy would've
hid $10 million in his own home?


01:05:03.900 --> 01:05:06.994
Miles was very
precise about things.


01:05:07.069 --> 01:05:09.060
Typical accountant,
I guess.


01:05:09.138 --> 01:05:13.165
Everything in its place,
and a place for everything.


01:05:13.242 --> 01:05:15.437
Don't move it.


01:05:17.647 --> 01:05:20.013
Chateau Hermitage '83.


01:05:20.650 --> 01:05:22.550
Do you know how much
that bottle costs?


01:05:22.618 --> 01:05:24.449
$1,000?


01:05:24.520 --> 01:05:27.455
That might pay
for the cork.


01:05:27.523 --> 01:05:30.287
This guy's probably got a
million-dollar wine collection.


01:05:50.746 --> 01:05:51.974
Wow.


01:05:52.848 --> 01:05:57.080
The place is temperature
controlled, fireproof probably.


01:05:59.121 --> 01:06:01.988
It's a great place
to hide $10 million.


01:06:02.058 --> 01:06:03.389
I would.


01:06:06.162 --> 01:06:07.891
But where?


01:06:10.900 --> 01:06:12.595
What are you doing?


01:06:12.668 --> 01:06:13.965
This rack just moved.


01:06:16.572 --> 01:06:18.199
Wait a minute.


01:06:26.048 --> 01:06:27.845
Oh, wow.


01:06:28.384 --> 01:06:29.749
Voila.


01:06:35.091 --> 01:06:36.991
Aren't you gonna
tell Hendricks?


01:06:37.059 --> 01:06:40.517
Just wanna take
a look inside first.


01:06:40.596 --> 01:06:41.620
I don't get it.


01:06:41.697 --> 01:06:43.028
Well, he's been
shutting me out.


01:06:43.099 --> 01:06:45.124
I just wanna
return the favor.


01:06:45.201 --> 01:06:47.260
Let's come back tonight.


01:06:49.305 --> 01:06:51.398
So how do we
pop that box?


01:06:51.474 --> 01:06:52.566
We'll google it.


01:06:52.641 --> 01:06:53.801
We think a lot alike.


01:06:53.876 --> 01:06:54.968
Is that right?


01:06:55.044 --> 01:06:56.341
Seriously,
we could be related.


01:07:13.863 --> 01:07:17.162
There's a very nice bottle of
Cabernet I'd like to show you.


01:07:17.233 --> 01:07:18.359
Good nose?


01:07:18.434 --> 01:07:19.526
Long finish.


01:07:19.602 --> 01:07:21.399
Mmm. I doubt
I can afford it.


01:07:21.470 --> 01:07:24.496
Oh, mademoiselle,
this one is on the house.


01:07:33.849 --> 01:07:35.476
You sure this will work?


01:07:35.551 --> 01:07:37.416
Always has.


01:07:41.257 --> 01:07:43.384
Wow, I got
software like that.


01:07:43.692 --> 01:07:45.626
For computers?
Yeah.


01:07:45.694 --> 01:07:47.161
And passwords?


01:07:47.229 --> 01:07:48.628
Yeah.


01:07:48.697 --> 01:07:49.686
Hmm.


01:07:49.999 --> 01:07:51.159
Maybe we are related.


01:07:51.233 --> 01:07:53.827
Next thing you know, you'll
be hitting me up for money.


01:07:55.771 --> 01:07:57.966
"I'll pay you back,
Uncle John. " Mmm-hmm.


01:07:59.508 --> 01:08:00.998
Sneaking out
the back door,


01:08:01.077 --> 01:08:04.444
showing up at barbecues
late, eating all the food.


01:08:04.547 --> 01:08:06.412
Oh, this is magic.


01:08:06.482 --> 01:08:09.576
Opened up like a little baby
on pamper day, didn't it?


01:08:16.192 --> 01:08:18.319
Okay, it won't
be long now.


01:08:18.394 --> 01:08:23.161
Just a couple of minutes, the
combination will show up right there.


01:08:31.307 --> 01:08:32.934
Any minute now.


01:08:46.655 --> 01:08:48.782
What do we do?


01:08:49.725 --> 01:08:51.784
Put it back together
and get outta here.


01:08:51.861 --> 01:08:53.158
Who sold you that thing?


01:08:53.229 --> 01:08:54.491
It's not the device.


01:08:54.563 --> 01:08:56.292
The device is good,
I've used it before.


01:08:56.365 --> 01:08:57.559
And how much did it cost?


01:08:57.633 --> 01:09:02.127
Me? Nothing. Uncle Sam, on the
other hand, paid $28,000 for it.


01:09:02.204 --> 01:09:03.899
Oh, my God.


01:09:03.973 --> 01:09:06.942
I have jacking software that
cost me $500, and it works.


01:09:07.009 --> 01:09:10.035
Well, it's a bit more
complicated than that. How?


01:09:10.112 --> 01:09:13.639
It's numbers, it's single-digit
and two-digit numbers.


01:09:13.716 --> 01:09:14.808
How hard could it be?


01:09:14.884 --> 01:09:17.045
A simple little combination,
and it can't come up with it?


01:09:17.119 --> 01:09:20.748
Well, this safe probably
has a five-number sequence.


01:09:20.823 --> 01:09:22.120
That's why it's
not working.


01:09:22.191 --> 01:09:23.453
What?


01:09:23.526 --> 01:09:26.859
99% of your containers
uses four or three numbers.


01:09:26.929 --> 01:09:28.692
This thing isn't programed
to do more than that.


01:09:28.764 --> 01:09:30.322
It can't do five numbers?


01:09:30.399 --> 01:09:31.923
No.


01:09:34.803 --> 01:09:37.067
Wait, it's a five-digit
combination. Five?


01:09:37.406 --> 01:09:38.873
Yes. Why?


01:09:38.941 --> 01:09:39.965
Turn that thing off.


01:09:40.042 --> 01:09:41.600
What?
Turn it off.


01:09:44.580 --> 01:09:49.108
When I hacked his computer, my
birthday was part of his password.


01:10:00.062 --> 01:10:02.189
Oh!
Nicely done.


01:10:02.264 --> 01:10:03.561
Let's keep it.


01:10:03.632 --> 01:10:04.963
Okay.


01:10:05.034 --> 01:10:06.899
What?
Just kidding.


01:10:06.969 --> 01:10:08.732
Yeah, me, too.


01:10:09.672 --> 01:10:11.799
Don't even
think about it.


01:10:11.874 --> 01:10:13.398
I'm not.


01:10:15.010 --> 01:10:16.500
Don't...


01:10:16.579 --> 01:10:18.513
I just wanna
touch it.


01:10:18.581 --> 01:10:20.572
And then you'll
wanna spend it.


01:10:20.649 --> 01:10:22.207
Do you hear that?


01:10:24.286 --> 01:10:25.685
It just called my name.


01:10:26.956 --> 01:10:29.754
"Rebecca. "


01:10:30.459 --> 01:10:32.427
That's just your
moral compass spinning.


01:10:32.494 --> 01:10:34.792
I am definitely
losing my balance.


01:10:34.863 --> 01:10:37.661
Then grab onto the walls.


01:10:38.367 --> 01:10:40.767
You need to get
me out of here.


01:10:40.836 --> 01:10:43.304
Seriously,
get me out of here.


01:10:43.372 --> 01:10:45.465
You definitely
got the fever, girl.


01:10:49.645 --> 01:10:51.943
NELSON: Once your eyes started
to glaze over, I got worried.


01:10:52.314 --> 01:10:55.283
Thanks for
pulling me outta there.


01:10:55.351 --> 01:10:58.047
I've been there.
I know how it feels.


01:10:58.120 --> 01:11:00.054
Ah... That much money...


01:11:00.122 --> 01:11:02.147
It's like the devil's
hand reaching out to you.


01:11:02.224 --> 01:11:03.987
I know.


01:11:07.229 --> 01:11:09.561
No, I don't think
your husband was


01:11:09.632 --> 01:11:11.725
planning on leaving
the night he was shot.


01:11:11.800 --> 01:11:12.994
Why not?


01:11:13.068 --> 01:11:14.933
$10 million is
a nice chunk of change,


01:11:15.004 --> 01:11:16.835
but stack it up
against a billion dollars


01:11:16.905 --> 01:11:18.270
in secret accounts


01:11:18.340 --> 01:11:20.308
just lying there
ready for the taking...


01:11:20.376 --> 01:11:22.844
But he could've accessed
Osterberg's accounts from anywhere.


01:11:22.911 --> 01:11:24.401
Not if he didn't
know where to look.


01:11:24.480 --> 01:11:26.675
The old coot had
the access codes


01:11:26.749 --> 01:11:28.580
hidden somewhere
we couldn't find.


01:11:28.651 --> 01:11:30.516
The only way
your husband could


01:11:30.586 --> 01:11:32.679
keep himself out ofjail
was to cooperate with us.


01:11:33.522 --> 01:11:36.457
So he could keep
looking for Osterberg's loot.


01:11:36.525 --> 01:11:38.823
And then somebody
had him killed...


01:11:38.894 --> 01:11:41.488
Which means there's
another player in the game.


01:11:41.563 --> 01:11:44.999
Killed Brigid,
wanted you dead, too.


01:11:45.067 --> 01:11:46.466
Why?


01:11:48.003 --> 01:11:49.903
Probably got to know you.


01:11:52.374 --> 01:11:54.103
'Cause you talk a lot.


01:11:58.547 --> 01:12:00.845
All right.
Get some rest.


01:12:00.916 --> 01:12:02.281
I got a mound of paperwork


01:12:02.351 --> 01:12:04.546
and conference calls
to get to in the morning.


01:12:07.489 --> 01:12:09.081
Stay in the hotel.


01:12:09.158 --> 01:12:10.625
Yes, master.


01:12:14.730 --> 01:12:18.393
A slave obeys his master.


01:12:34.483 --> 01:12:35.745
Hello?


01:12:36.952 --> 01:12:38.351
Who?


01:12:42.458 --> 01:12:44.392
Ah, screw this.


01:12:50.165 --> 01:12:51.530
REBECCA: Hello.


01:12:51.600 --> 01:12:52.760
Where are you?


01:12:52.835 --> 01:12:53.995
Out and about.


01:12:54.069 --> 01:12:56.333
I told you to
stay at the hotel.


01:12:56.405 --> 01:12:59.841
Osterberg offered me
an exclusive interview.


01:12:59.908 --> 01:13:03.241
Rebecca, you know all he wants
is to find out what you know.


01:13:03.312 --> 01:13:05.212
Of course,
but a world exclusive


01:13:05.280 --> 01:13:07.544
with this guy will
get me my job back.


01:13:08.183 --> 01:13:09.377
You got fired?


01:13:09.451 --> 01:13:10.611
Sort of.


01:13:10.686 --> 01:13:14.053
It's hard to say.
I might have quit.


01:13:14.123 --> 01:13:15.715
I'm not sure now.


01:13:15.791 --> 01:13:17.782
Do you ever follow the rules?


01:13:17.860 --> 01:13:19.054
I'm a woman.


01:13:19.128 --> 01:13:20.595
What does that mean?


01:13:20.662 --> 01:13:23.290
I don't know. It
sounds good, doesn't it?


01:13:25.434 --> 01:13:27.334
Be careful.


01:13:27.403 --> 01:13:29.735
Call me when you're done.


01:13:44.219 --> 01:13:47.313
I'm getting it
authenticated later today.


01:13:47.389 --> 01:13:50.790
Beautiful piece. Whose
pension fund paid for it?


01:13:50.859 --> 01:13:53.987
Innocent until proven guilty,
Rebecca. You should know that.


01:13:54.062 --> 01:13:56.997
I know about jackals
that feed on the weak.


01:13:57.065 --> 01:14:00.933
We do tend to romanticize
that part of it, don't we?


01:14:01.003 --> 01:14:04.200
People like you make
investments to make money.


01:14:04.306 --> 01:14:07.104
For you to make money,
someone has to lose it.


01:14:07.176 --> 01:14:09.508
How much do you think
you're worth at the moment?


01:14:09.578 --> 01:14:12.945
Who knows? It's hard to say.
It changes from day to day.


01:14:13.015 --> 01:14:15.210
But if I had to guess, I'd
have to say a billion or so.


01:14:15.284 --> 01:14:16.273
Would you like a drink?


01:14:18.320 --> 01:14:21.118
I'm on my way to a meeting,
Inspector. What can I do for you?


01:14:21.190 --> 01:14:22.851
Forgive me, Commissioner.


01:14:22.925 --> 01:14:26.224
The wife of Osterberg's
former associate was murdered.


01:14:26.295 --> 01:14:27.922
There have been two
attempts on the life of


01:14:27.996 --> 01:14:29.987
a reporter who's
investigating his activities,


01:14:30.065 --> 01:14:32.966
and an FBl agent was almost
killed in an explosion.


01:14:33.035 --> 01:14:34.297
It all points
back to Osterberg.


01:14:34.369 --> 01:14:35.597
So what do you recommend?


01:14:35.671 --> 01:14:37.639
At the very least, I'd like to
bring him in for questioning,


01:14:37.706 --> 01:14:39.799
make him worry that his
house arrest could be revoked.


01:14:39.875 --> 01:14:41.172
I think it'll
shake things up a bit.


01:14:45.347 --> 01:14:47.372
So what else can I tell you?


01:14:47.449 --> 01:14:48.575
How do you
really feel about


01:14:48.650 --> 01:14:50.709
the people that lost
everything because of


01:14:50.786 --> 01:14:52.481
what happened
with your company?


01:14:52.554 --> 01:14:55.421
Well, as I said before,
people make investments.


01:14:55.491 --> 01:14:59.484
Sometimes they work,
and sometimes they fail.


01:14:59.561 --> 01:15:00.823
Please, come on.


01:15:00.896 --> 01:15:03.194
Show me the real
Ronald Osterberg.


01:15:03.799 --> 01:15:05.391
All right.


01:15:05.467 --> 01:15:08.561
I'll answer some of your questions
if you answer some of mine.


01:15:09.938 --> 01:15:12.065
Deal.


01:15:12.140 --> 01:15:13.835
You go first.


01:15:14.042 --> 01:15:15.634
All right.


01:15:16.078 --> 01:15:17.375
How do I really feel


01:15:17.446 --> 01:15:20.313
about those poor
unfortunate masses


01:15:20.549 --> 01:15:23.177
of greedy, grasping,
small-minded folk


01:15:23.285 --> 01:15:25.515
in their pathetic
little houses


01:15:25.587 --> 01:15:27.782
in their pathetic
little neighborhoods,


01:15:27.856 --> 01:15:29.847
sitting in front
of their televisions,


01:15:29.925 --> 01:15:31.893
drinking their
Bud Light and watching


01:15:31.960 --> 01:15:34.190
the reality of a world
that doesn't exist?


01:15:34.263 --> 01:15:36.163
How do I feel
about them?


01:15:36.231 --> 01:15:38.631
I don't care whether
they live or die.


01:15:38.700 --> 01:15:40.691
Stuff 'em.


01:15:41.436 --> 01:15:43.904
Wow! You are disgusting.


01:15:43.972 --> 01:15:45.837
But you're attracted
to me, anyway.


01:15:45.908 --> 01:15:48.968
No, no.
I'm fascinated.


01:15:49.044 --> 01:15:53.344
You mustn't mistake that
for desire or empathy.


01:15:53.415 --> 01:15:56.213
It's like I have a true
monster under the microscope.


01:15:58.020 --> 01:16:00.648
I'll take that as
a compliment. Drink?


01:16:00.722 --> 01:16:01.916
No.


01:16:01.990 --> 01:16:03.890
My turn to ask
the questions.


01:16:04.793 --> 01:16:06.226
What is it that
you wanna know?


01:16:06.695 --> 01:16:09.027
Have you found
my money yet?


01:16:09.565 --> 01:16:11.658
If we had,
I wouldn't tell you.


01:16:12.234 --> 01:16:14.099
We'll get back to that.


01:16:16.939 --> 01:16:19.635
What about Brigid Archer?
Poor Brigid.


01:16:19.708 --> 01:16:22.108
Now, why would
I want her dead?


01:16:22.644 --> 01:16:27.206
Well, you send someone to look
for your money, she got in the way.


01:16:27.382 --> 01:16:28.872
I see.


01:16:37.125 --> 01:16:39.616
I think someone's trying
to get me out of the way.


01:16:39.928 --> 01:16:42.055
The boat, Brigid,
all of it.


01:16:42.130 --> 01:16:45.224
All arranged to make it
look like I was responsible.


01:16:46.902 --> 01:16:48.699
So you think
you're being framed.


01:16:49.338 --> 01:16:51.465
I do have enemies,
as you can imagine.


01:17:00.649 --> 01:17:04.050
My, this is a big
day for visitors.


01:17:06.121 --> 01:17:09.090
Ronald Osterberg,
you're under arrest.


01:17:09.157 --> 01:17:13.651
Indeed. I'm under house
arrest pending my appeal.


01:17:13.729 --> 01:17:16.095
I have not violated
any of the conditions


01:17:16.164 --> 01:17:18.632
of my bail, so I'm not going anywhere.


01:17:18.700 --> 01:17:22.192
This is a fresh charge. Conspiracy
in the murder of Brigid Archer.


01:17:22.738 --> 01:17:24.330
You'll be taken away
to police headquarters


01:17:24.406 --> 01:17:25.771
where you'll be
formally arraigned.


01:17:25.841 --> 01:17:27.365
You have the right
to remain silent.


01:17:27.442 --> 01:17:30.002
Anything you do, say, may be
used against you in evidence.


01:17:30.078 --> 01:17:33.741
This is outrageous. I had
nothing to do with that.


01:17:33.815 --> 01:17:35.840
Take him away.


01:17:36.018 --> 01:17:38.578
Someone is trying very hard
to get me out of the way.


01:17:38.654 --> 01:17:40.679
Find out who and
I'll make you rich.


01:17:44.760 --> 01:17:46.819
I'm not even gonna ask
what you're doing here.


01:17:46.895 --> 01:17:48.487
I'm trying to find out
who killed my husband.


01:17:48.563 --> 01:17:52.624
No, you're just after a scoop.
Your kind make me sick.


01:17:52.701 --> 01:17:54.794
You know, it's possible you're
looking at the wrong guy.


01:17:54.870 --> 01:17:58.067
What did he promise you?
How much?


01:18:00.108 --> 01:18:02.372
Leave now before
I arrest you, too.


01:18:06.448 --> 01:18:08.439
This is Hendricks.


01:18:08.517 --> 01:18:12.078
Round up the staff,
security. I want everyone out.


01:18:12.154 --> 01:18:16.386
Nobody comes back here for
anything. Am I clear on that?


01:18:40.649 --> 01:18:41.707
Nelson.


01:18:41.783 --> 01:18:42.772
REBECCA: Hey, it's me.


01:18:42.851 --> 01:18:44.341
They just arrested Osterberg.


01:18:44.419 --> 01:18:45.545
Why?


01:18:45.620 --> 01:18:47.247
Brigid Archer's murder.


01:18:47.322 --> 01:18:48.846
Really? Hmm.


01:18:49.324 --> 01:18:50.450
Where are you?


01:18:50.525 --> 01:18:52.459
Just down from his place.


01:18:52.527 --> 01:18:54.290
They ran everyone
out of the house,


01:18:54.463 --> 01:18:57.057
staff, security, everyone.


01:18:57.132 --> 01:18:58.929
He's no flight risk.


01:18:59.000 --> 01:19:01.059
He'll make bail in 24 hours.


01:19:01.136 --> 01:19:03.900
In the meantime,
his place will be empty.


01:19:08.043 --> 01:19:10.273
NELSON: Come on, I got you.


01:19:14.649 --> 01:19:15.809
It's too far.


01:19:15.884 --> 01:19:17.010
Come on, I got you.


01:19:17.652 --> 01:19:18.744
How much do you weigh, girl?


01:19:18.820 --> 01:19:20.811
A hundred and... What do
you mean how much do I weigh?


01:19:20.889 --> 01:19:23.449
Come on. Maybe you should
start hitting the gym.


01:19:50.218 --> 01:19:51.879
This place is huge.


01:19:51.953 --> 01:19:53.420
Where do you think
we should start?


01:20:26.888 --> 01:20:27.980
Nelson.


01:20:28.056 --> 01:20:30.490
Inspector Hendricks,
what a surprise.


01:20:30.559 --> 01:20:32.493
Now, look, this is an official police...


01:20:32.928 --> 01:20:34.418
Back up.


01:20:34.496 --> 01:20:35.963
Turn around.


01:20:39.234 --> 01:20:40.724
Miles?


01:20:41.536 --> 01:20:43.800
Hello, darling.


01:20:45.407 --> 01:20:48.103
What are you doing?


01:20:48.810 --> 01:20:51.643
Just trying to
make a living.


01:20:52.347 --> 01:20:53.473
Shoot him.


01:20:54.549 --> 01:20:56.176
Take it easy.
I mean it. Shoot him.


01:20:56.251 --> 01:20:57.343
Right, hang on.


01:20:57.419 --> 01:20:59.751
Put your hands
where I can see them.


01:21:01.823 --> 01:21:03.586
I gotta give it
to you, Archer.


01:21:03.658 --> 01:21:06.559
That performance on the
marina, pretty convincing.


01:21:06.628 --> 01:21:07.959
Stay where you're at.
I'm coming to you.


01:21:08.029 --> 01:21:09.053
Please hurry.


01:21:13.034 --> 01:21:14.797
Played you for a sucker,
didn't we?


01:21:15.737 --> 01:21:17.261
Don't tell him anything.


01:21:17.339 --> 01:21:20.433
Well, it really doesn't
matter now, does it?


01:21:20.508 --> 01:21:21.907
Letting someone
shoot your finger off


01:21:21.977 --> 01:21:23.410
is worth a billion,
don't you think?


01:21:23.478 --> 01:21:26.777
Now, the blood was mine,
but the bullets were blanks.


01:21:26.848 --> 01:21:27.974
No. Don't shoot.


01:21:32.454 --> 01:21:34.615
Two years of watching Scrooge
count his money,


01:21:34.689 --> 01:21:36.748
and the old
fool never realized


01:21:36.825 --> 01:21:39.055
I knew where he kept this.
Billion dollars.


01:21:39.127 --> 01:21:41.755
Access codes,
global accounts, everything.


01:21:42.197 --> 01:21:44.859
Brigid did her
part well enough,


01:21:44.933 --> 01:21:47.800
but in the end,
she got greedy, so adios.


01:21:47.869 --> 01:21:49.803
We can make
a deal here, Nelson,


01:21:49.871 --> 01:21:51.736
something to make
everyone happy.


01:21:51.806 --> 01:21:52.898
Oh, is that right?


01:21:52.974 --> 01:21:55.909
Hey, we're talking
about a lot of money.


01:21:56.344 --> 01:21:59.040
A billion dollars
split four ways.


01:21:59.114 --> 01:22:01.480
You miserable puke.


01:22:01.549 --> 01:22:03.244
I can't believe
I ever loved you.


01:22:03.318 --> 01:22:06.515
Rebecca, you have to look at
the bigger picture, sweetie.


01:22:06.588 --> 01:22:08.783
You are a thief
and a murderer.


01:22:09.324 --> 01:22:11.315
And your point is?


01:22:12.093 --> 01:22:15.290
Look, I can give you guys
$10 million in cash right now.


01:22:15.363 --> 01:22:16.557
Shut up, Dennis.


01:22:16.631 --> 01:22:17.996
It's at my house.


01:22:18.066 --> 01:22:19.966
We already know
where the money is.


01:22:20.035 --> 01:22:22.731
Well, then take it. You go
your way, and we'll go...


01:22:22.804 --> 01:22:24.704
$10 million?
What $10 million?


01:22:24.773 --> 01:22:26.798
Shh! That's chump change
compared to what we have here.


01:22:26.875 --> 01:22:28.740
All right, that's enough.
Let's go.


01:22:28.843 --> 01:22:30.208
THUG 1: Drop it.


01:22:32.714 --> 01:22:34.204
Turn around.


01:22:37.152 --> 01:22:39.518
If he tries anything,
shoot her.


01:22:39.587 --> 01:22:42.055
You really are a putz,
Hendricks.


01:22:43.491 --> 01:22:44.788
Bring the car around.


01:22:44.859 --> 01:22:46.349
Back it up and
open the trunk.


01:22:46.428 --> 01:22:47.952
Follow me.


01:22:48.029 --> 01:22:49.189
Move.


01:22:50.432 --> 01:22:51.626
Run! Run!


01:22:53.568 --> 01:22:55.035
The key's in my pocket.
Okay.


01:22:55.603 --> 01:22:58.697
You two go around the back.
I'll take care of this one.


01:23:00.442 --> 01:23:01.909
Put it in my hand.


01:23:01.977 --> 01:23:03.103
Go.


01:23:03.178 --> 01:23:04.577
No.
Go, go!


01:23:29.571 --> 01:23:31.334
How's that feel, Mr. G-Man?


01:23:31.406 --> 01:23:33.135
Feels great.


01:23:38.046 --> 01:23:39.377
Stop!


01:23:44.886 --> 01:23:46.751
You wanna know
what FBl stands for?


01:23:47.288 --> 01:23:49.848
Fumble bumble incompetent.


01:24:16.384 --> 01:24:19.979
No. No, please. Please.


01:24:25.560 --> 01:24:27.926
Time to have
some fun, baby.


01:24:55.957 --> 01:24:57.083
Ah!


01:25:30.024 --> 01:25:31.855
Becca, Becca.


01:25:31.926 --> 01:25:34.690
Becca, put it down.


01:25:41.102 --> 01:25:43.366
I have sacrificed
everything,


01:25:43.438 --> 01:25:45.338
but I tried to
keep you out of this.


01:25:48.009 --> 01:25:50.375
Billionaires run
the world, baby.


01:25:50.445 --> 01:25:51.571
We can be a part of that.


01:26:00.255 --> 01:26:02.280
I know you never
stopped loving me.


01:26:05.193 --> 01:26:07.491
Come on, come on.
You're not gonna shoot me.


01:26:07.929 --> 01:26:09.328
The hell I'm not.


01:26:21.376 --> 01:26:23.435
Now you're really dead.


01:26:31.886 --> 01:26:34.514
It's okay, it's okay.
It's okay, it's over.


01:26:35.190 --> 01:26:36.680
It's over, come on.


01:26:37.859 --> 01:26:40.487
NEWS REPORTER: Accused Australian
financier Ronald Osterberg


01:26:40.562 --> 01:26:43.929
lost his battle today against
extradition to the United States,


01:26:43.998 --> 01:26:46.831
where he faces billion-dollar
embezzlement charges.


01:26:46.901 --> 01:26:49.335
Police and FBI have
recovered access codes


01:26:49.404 --> 01:26:53.238
to secret accounts that contained
much of the stolen funds.


01:26:53.875 --> 01:26:56.139
It was nice
working with you.


01:26:56.211 --> 01:26:57.508
You mean that?
No.


01:26:57.579 --> 01:26:58.671
I saved your life.


01:26:58.746 --> 01:27:00.304
Oh, yeah, and how many
times did I save yours?


01:27:00.381 --> 01:27:01.643
That's your job.


01:27:02.984 --> 01:27:04.576
You gonna write
about all of this?


01:27:04.852 --> 01:27:06.319
Of course.


01:27:06.454 --> 01:27:07.887
Just don't use my name.


01:27:07.956 --> 01:27:08.980
Why not?


01:27:09.057 --> 01:27:10.820
People find out
I let you tag along,


01:27:10.892 --> 01:27:12.917
I'll be a traffic cop
within a week.


01:27:13.194 --> 01:27:15.424
Hey, I was invaluable.


01:27:15.496 --> 01:27:17.327
Yeah, and ready
to steal $10 million.


01:27:17.398 --> 01:27:19.559
Okay, yeah, but...


01:27:19.734 --> 01:27:21.292
Ba... ba... ba.


01:27:21.502 --> 01:27:23.129
Yeah, but that's all I got.


01:27:23.204 --> 01:27:25.866
Exactly. You'd have
taken that money.


01:27:25.940 --> 01:27:29.398
Just a finder's fee, 10%.
I mean, who would've known?


01:27:30.311 --> 01:27:31.938
5%.


01:27:32.013 --> 01:27:34.106
Oh, well then, just 5%.


01:27:35.350 --> 01:27:36.783
You got the fever, girl.


01:27:36.851 --> 01:27:38.250
I do not.


01:27:38.319 --> 01:27:39.946
You're gonna
like my story.


01:27:40.021 --> 01:27:41.283
Good Lord.


01:27:41.356 --> 01:27:43.722
And we can discuss
it over breakfast.


01:27:43.791 --> 01:27:45.190
Breakfast, huh?


01:27:45.293 --> 01:27:47.693
We won't be fighting
over that bill.

